"""Live counterfactual laboratory dashboard, served alongside the observer."""
PAGE = '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Live market ecology laboratory</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;background:#0e1726;color:#edf4ff;margin:25px auto;max-width:1150px;padding:20px}a{color:#7fdfda}p{line-height:1.6;color:#bfcee1}.panel{background:#1a2a40;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;margin:18px 0}.cards{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}.card{flex:1;min-width:180px}.big{font-size:26px;font-weight:bold}canvas{width:100%;height:330px}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;white-space:nowrap}th,td{padding:10px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #3d536e}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}select{padding:9px;background:#263d58;color:white}li{margin:10px 0;line-height:1.5}.badge{color:#ffd88a}</style><h1>Live market ecology laboratory</h1><p><a href="/">Live order book</a> · <span class="badge">Live observations + simulated interventions</span></p><p>Start with the real Bitcoin book. Ask what would happen if a simulated participant bought or sold, makers removed liquidity, or a dealer hedged an assumed gamma position. Each experiment uses its own copy of the book. These are immediate modeled effects, not predictions or observed participant activity.</p><div id="status" class="panel">Connecting…</div><div class="panel cards"><div class="card">Observed midpoint<div id="mid" class="big">—</div></div><div class="card">60-second illustrative Monte Carlo range<div id="mc" class="big">Warming up</div><p id="mcinfo"></p></div></div><div class="panel"><label>Compare with live price: <select id="series"><option value="large_buy_mid">Simulated 10 BTC buy</option><option value="thin_buy_mid">10 BTC buy with half the liquidity</option></select></label><canvas id="chart"></canvas><p>Teal: observed midpoint. Orange: counterfactual midpoint if that intervention happened at each sampled moment. Orange points are independent experiments, not a simulated trading trajectory.</p></div><div class="panel scroll"><h2>How much does each intervention move the book?</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Simulated intervention</th><th>Filled BTC</th><th>Unfilled BTC</th><th>Buy/sell VWAP</th><th>Hedge BTC (+ buy)</th><th>Midpoint change USDT</th><th>Change bps</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table><p>If known liquidity is exhausted, the price effect is unknown. We do not invent deeper liquidity. No latency, replenishment, hidden orders, venue routing or maker queue fills are modeled here.</p></div><div class="panel"><h2>30-second simulated participant ecology</h2><p>A fresh live book initializes each experiment every 10 seconds. All three scenarios receive the same synthetic arrival tape. These paths run in simulated time, not future live time.</p><canvas id="rollchart"></canvas><p>Teal: baseline · Orange: maker B withdraws at 10–20s · Purple: assumed short gamma. A fixed simulated institution buys 1 BTC at 10s and sells 1 BTC at 20s.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Baseline simulated role</th><th>Final inventory BTC</th><th>Cash change USDT</th><th>Marked wealth USDT</th></tr></thead><tbody id="agents"></tbody></table></div><p id="rollinfo"></p></div><div class="panel"><h2>What the models mean</h2><ul id="models"></ul><p>Book impact: consume displayed levels in price order. Gamma hedge: ΔH = −Γ × ΔS. Monte Carlo: S(T) = S(0) exp(−σ²T/2 + σ√T Z), using rolling one-second log returns. It assumes zero expected price drift and constant volatility.</p></div><script>let data;const f=x=>x==null?'—':Number(x).toFixed(3);function chart(){let el=document.getElementById('chart');el.width=el.clientWidth;el.height=330;let c=el.getContext('2d');if(!data)return;let rows=data.history.filter(x=>x.time_ms>=Date.now()-120000),key=document.getElementById('series').value,values=rows.flatMap(x=>[x.observed_mid,x[key]]).filter(x=>x!=null);if(!values.length)return;let lo=Math.min(...values),hi=Math.max(...values);if(hi===lo){lo-=.1;hi+=.1}let t0=rows[0].time_ms,t1=rows.at(-1).time_ms;c.fillStyle='#bfcee1';c.fillText(f(hi)+' USDT',5,15);c.fillText(f(lo)+' USDT',5,325);for(let [k,color] of [['observed_mid','#73d8cf'],[key,'#ffb267']]){c.strokeStyle=color;c.beginPath();let active=false,previous=null;for(let r of rows){if(r[k]==null||previous!=null&&r.time_ms-previous>1500)active=false;if(r[k]!=null){let x=20+(r.time_ms-t0)/Math.max(1,t1-t0)*(el.width-40),y=25+(hi-r[k])/(hi-lo)*280;active?c.lineTo(x,y):c.moveTo(x,y);active=true}previous=r.time_ms}c.stroke()}}function rolloutChart(){let el=document.getElementById('rollchart');el.width=el.clientWidth;el.height=330;let c=el.getContext('2d'),r=data.rollouts,vals=['baseline','withdrawal','short_gamma'].flatMap(k=>r[k].trace.map(x=>x.move_bps)).filter(x=>x!=null);if(!vals.length)return;let lo=Math.min(...vals),hi=Math.max(...vals);if(hi===lo){lo-=.1;hi+=.1}c.fillStyle='#bfcee1';c.fillText('Modeled midpoint change: '+f(lo)+' to '+f(hi)+' bps · 0–29 simulated seconds',10,15);for(let [key,color] of [['baseline','#73d8cf'],['withdrawal','#ffb267'],['short_gamma','#cc9cff']]){c.beginPath();c.strokeStyle=color;let active=false;for(let row of r[key].trace){if(row.move_bps==null){active=false;continue}let x=20+row.second/29*(el.width-40),y=25+(hi-row.move_bps)/(hi-lo)*280;active?c.lineTo(x,y):c.moveTo(x,y);active=true}c.stroke()}document.getElementById('agents').innerHTML=r.baseline.participants.map(p=>`<tr><td>${p.role}</td><td>${f(p.inventory_btc)}</td><td>${f(p.cash_usdt)}</td><td>${f(p.marked_wealth_usdt)}</td></tr>`).join('');document.getElementById('rollinfo').textContent='Initialized at '+new Date(r.generated_ns/1e6).toISOString()+'. '+r.baseline.assumptions+' Baseline paid fees: '+f(r.baseline.total_paid_fees_usdt)+' USDT. Marked wealth is not realized exit profit.'}function clear(reason){document.getElementById('status').textContent=reason;document.getElementById('mid').textContent='—';document.getElementById('mc').textContent='Unavailable';document.getElementById('mcinfo').textContent='';document.getElementById('rows').textContent='';data=null;chart();document.getElementById('agents').textContent='';document.getElementById('rollinfo').textContent='';let rc=document.getElementById('rollchart');rc.getContext('2d').clearRect(0,0,rc.width,rc.height)}async function draw(){try{let response=await fetch('ecology.json',{cache:'no-store'});if(!response.ok)throw Error('unavailable');let s=await response.json();if(s.mode!=='replay'&&(Date.now()-s.generated_ns/1e6>2000||Date.now()-s.generated_ns/1e6<0)){clear('Observer offline or clock mismatch · experiments paused');return}document.getElementById('models').replaceChildren(...Object.entries(s.models).map(([k,v])=>{let li=document.createElement('li');li.textContent=v;return li}));if(s.status!=='running'){clear('Experiments paused · '+s.reason);return}data=s;document.getElementById('status').textContent='Running on a fresh synchronized book · source update '+s.source_update_id+' · roles and gamma are assumptions';document.getElementById('mid').textContent=f(s.observed_mid)+' USDT';let m=s.monte_carlo;document.getElementById('mc').textContent=m.status==='warming_up'?'Warming up '+m.samples+'/'+m.required:f(m.p05)+' – '+f(m.p95);document.getElementById('mcinfo').textContent=m.status==='warming_up'?'Requires 61 consecutive fresh one-second samples.':m.caveat+' '+m.return_samples+' rolling returns; 1,000 paths.';document.getElementById('rows').innerHTML=s.scenarios.map(r=>`<tr><td>${r.name}</td><td>${f(r.initiating_filled_btc)}</td><td>${f(r.initiating_unfilled_btc)}</td><td>${f(r.initiating_vwap)}</td><td>${f(r.hedge_signed_btc)}</td><td>${f(r.move_usdt)}</td><td>${f(r.move_bps)}</td></tr>`).join('');chart();rolloutChart()}catch(e){clear('Cannot load experiments')}}document.getElementById('series').onchange=chart;addEventListener('resize',chart);draw();setInterval(draw,1000)</script></html>'''
